\description{
Tidy readers and writers so you rarely need \code{sf::st_read()},
\code{terra::rast()}, or raw GDAL utilities. \code{\link[=geo_read]{geo_read()}} auto-detects raster
versus vector from the file extension (and GDAL driver when needed).
\code{\link[=geo_write]{geo_write()}} picks a writer from the object type and the destination
extension. Format-specific twins \code{\link[=geo_vector_read]{geo_vector_read()}} / \code{\link[=geo_vector_write]{geo_vector_write()}}
and \code{\link[=geo_raster_read]{geo_raster_read()}} / \code{\link[=geo_raster_write]{geo_raster_write()}} are available when you
already know the type. All I/O goes through \strong{sf} and \strong{terra} (GDAL /
OGR under the hood). Do not use the retired \strong{rgdal} package.

